  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eDover\u0026#39;s stitch in Morris Canal Greenway\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Dover portion of the towpath is envisioned as part of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.morriscanalgreenway.org/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eMorris Canal Greenway\u003c/a\u003e,  a 111-mile walking and bicycle trail that\u0026#39;s still being assembled across six North Jersey counties from the Delaware on the west to the Hudson on the east. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe project \u0026#34;is transforming our northern New Jersey communities into more pedestrian-friendly, environmentally conscious areas, all while reducing our dependency on cars,\u0026#34; said Dover Mayor James Dodd. \u0026#34;As the mayor of one of the most densely populated towns in our county, we envision a community that focuses on and emphasizes these initiatives while celebrating our history, and this is just the start.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eSeveral segments of the Greenway have already been completed, but much work remains to create a continuous trail,\u0026#34; according to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://canalsocietynj.org/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eCanal Society of New Jersey\u003c/a\u003e, which is based in Stanhope. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Dover Towpath will connect to a trail in Wharton and hopefully encourage more use of the underutilized Waterworks Park, Dover officials said. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFunded in part by a $50,000 T-Mobile grant, officials worked with the Morris County Park Commission and local students in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.dailyrecord.com/story/news/local/2019/11/30/first-generation-dover-students-get-aid-support-college/4299520002/\"\u003eDover College Promise\u003c/a\u003e program to design and build the towpath. The Canal Society provided an additional $10,000 grant to cover the costs and donated historical signage.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMorris Canal history \u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe canal was constructed from 1825 to 1831 to transport coal from Pennsylvania\u0026#39;s Lehigh Valley to customers in New Jersey and New York. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBuilt by the Morris Canal \u0026amp; Banking Co., the 102-mile waterway \u0026#34;would pass through the heart of New Jersey’s iron district and provide the long-needed transportation system that would create new commercial activity and enable rustic settlements like Dover and Rockaway to grow into thriving industrial towns,\u0026#34; according to the Canal Society\u0026#39;s website.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "993000002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBy the 1880s, however, railroads had rendered canals obsolete. The automobile struck the final blow, and the Morris Canal was formally abandoned in 1924. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eSince then, portions of the channel have been dismantled or destroyed. But some towpaths and other historical remnants have been preserved or repurposed. Approximately 20 miles of path are planned for or already exist in Passaic County. Last year, Newark was awarded a $769,000 state grant for the second phase of the Newark Morris Canal Bikeway project. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe North Jersey Transportation Planning Authority, in partnership with the Canal Society and the Morris Canal Working Group have presented a plan for a continuous trail that closely follows the historic canal route. The greenway would begin in Phillipsburg, end in Jersey City and in between run through Morris, Sussex, Warren, Passaic, Essex and Hudson counties.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eWilliam Westhoven is a local reporter for DailyRecord.com. For unlimited access to the most important news from your local community, \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://cm.dailyrecord.com/specialoffer/?gps-source\u003dCPNAVBARBBB\u0026utm_medium\u003dONSITE\u0026utm_campaign\u003d2019SLJP10\u0026utm_content\u003dCPNAVBARBBB\u0026utm_source\u003dCPNAVBARBBB\u0026onSuccessRedirectURL\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.dailyrecord.com%2F\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eplease subscribe or activate your digital account today\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eEmail: \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"mailto:wwesthoven@gannettnj.com\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003ewwesthoven@\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003edailyrecord.com Twitter/X: \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://twitter.com/wwesthoven?s\u003d17\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e@wwesthoven\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73976509007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIndependence Day will be here before we know it, so it\u0026#39;s time to start planning how you\u0026#39;d like to celebrate. And, while attending a family gathering or a backyard barbecue could be fun, there\u0026#39;s nothing quite like ringing in the Fourth of July with some fireworks, parades, festivals and more.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBecause North Jersey has celebrations taking place in every corner of the region, we\u0026#39;ve compiled a list of the currently scheduled events to make your life easier.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd you won\u0026#39;t want to miss the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.macys.com/s/fireworks/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ethe 48th Annual Macy\u0026#39;s Fourth of July Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. While this event is technically in New York City, the Macy\u0026#39;s July 4th fireworks will \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/new-jersey/2024/04/30/macys-july-4th-fireworks-return-hudson-river-nj-nyc/73518682007/\"\u003etake place on the Hudson River for the first time since 2013\u003c/a\u003e, meaning New Jersey residents can view them from places like Hoboken, Jersey City and Weehawken. The show begins at 8 p.m. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHere\u0026#39;s a look at the Fourth of July events and firework shows taking place across North Jersey in 2024, by location.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003eWant to see them filtered by date? Head on over to our other story: \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/21/fourth-of-july-fireworks-2024-north-jersey-things-to-do/73640506007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/21/fourth-of-july-fireworks-2024-north-jersey-things-to-do/73640506007/\"\u003eWhen are North Jersey fireworks?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBergen County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eCresskill\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cresskillboro.com/index.php/component/fileman/?view\u003dfile\u0026routed\u003d1\u0026itemless\u003d1\u0026name\u003dJuly%204th%20Celebration%202024.pdf\u0026folder\u003d2024/06\u0026container\u003dfileman-files\"\u003e4th of July Townwide Celebration\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e. On July 4 (rain date July 5), enjoy a day of fun, food, rides, games, a D.J. and more. Call the Recreation Office at 201-816-8065 or jmitchell@cresskillboro.org for information. Cresskill residents only. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e 10 a.m. to 1 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eCommunity Center, 100 Third St.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eEast Rutherford\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://playmeadowlands.com/event/fan-appreciation-fireworks-night/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMeadowlands Fireworks \u0026amp; Fan Appreciation Night\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. At Fan Appreciation Night at Meadowlands Racetrack on July 6you enjoy $1 concession items, $2 Bud and Bud Light drafts, as well as a free fireworks show for July 4th after the races. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e6 to 11:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eMeadowlands Racetrack, 1 Racetrack Drive, East Rutherford.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eEdgewater\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.edgewaternj.org/CivicAlerts.aspx?AID\u003d387\"\u003eIndependence Day Fireworks\u003c/a\u003e. Fireworks, live music, food trucks and kids activities on June 27. Bring a chair or blanket. Parking is limited, so attendees are encouraged to use the free River Road shuttle bus. The rain date is June 30. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e 6 to 10 p.m. Fireworks begin at approximately 9:20. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Veterans Field, 1057-1165 River Road.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eFair Lawn\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.fairlawn.org/p/holiday-events\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFair Lawn Fireworks Show\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Fair Lawn will be hosting their annual fireworks show on June 27. In addition to fireworks, there will be food vendors and live music for guests to enjoy. Tickets for the pre-fireworks festivities are $5 for children under 12 and seniors, $7 for adults and $25 for a family of five. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eGates for the event open at 6:45 p.m., and fireworks begin at sundown. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eMemorial Park, Berdan Avenue and 1st Street, Fair Lawn.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGlen Rock\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"http://www.glenrockpops.org\"\u003ePops Celebrates Nation’s Birthday\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/strong\u003e The Pops Orchestra goes patriotic on July 3 with a free concert on the lawn of Borough Hall. Bring chairs and blankets, and enjoy the music that will include an evening of marches, popular patriotic songs and light classics under the baton of music director Anthony LaGruth. Meet the grand marshals – Marcia, Walter and Daniel Perry - of the July 4 parade as well. The IDA raffle drawing will take place during the intermission, with prizes including a $500 Visa gift card and a $250 Shop the Rock basket of gift cards from town merchants. Tickets will be available for purchase at Kilroy’s prior to the concert or at Borough Hall that night. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eConcert begins at 7 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eBorough Hall, 1 Harding Plaza.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHere Comes the Parade on July 4th.\u003c/strong\u003e Rain or shine, there will be marching bands, pipers, historic Civil War reenactors, floats, clowns and more. For information, write to grparade@icloud.com. \u003cstrong\u003eHours\u003c/strong\u003e: The parade kicks off at 9:30 a.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e The route begins at Glen Rock High School, 400 Hamilton Ave., and goes east on Harristown Road, takes a left on Highland Road, another left at Rock Road through the center of town, and a right on Doremus Avenue, ending at the Municipal Pool parking lot. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLeonia\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.co.bergen.nj.us/public-information/press-releases/768-county-nj-wind-symphony-partner-to-bring-4th-of-july-concert-fireworks-to-overpeck-county-park\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBergen County\u0026#39;s Star-Spangled Spectacular\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. This Independence Day celebration on July 4 will feature the New Jersey Wind Symphony, other live entertainment, children\u0026#39;s activities, food trucks, a beer and wine garden and fireworks at Overpeck Creek. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 5 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eOverpeck County Park, 40 Fort Lee Road, Leonia.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLyndhurst\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://allevents.in/lyndhurst/zappy-4th-of-july/200026427019623#google_vignette\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLyndhurst\u0026#39;s Zappy Fourth of July\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. At the Lyndhurst Band Shell, there will be a free concert on July 4 with several different performers to celebrate the Fourth of July. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e 7:30 to 9 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eLyndhurst Municipal Park, 367 Valley Brook Ave., Lyndhurst.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eParamus\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7862975002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.paramus4thofjuly.com/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eParamus 4th of July Fireworks Show\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Paramus will be hosting their annual 4th of July fireworks show on June 30. Prior to the fireworks show, there will be live entertainment and food vendors. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e The time of the event is to be determined. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Cliff Gennarelli Sports Complex, Garden State Plaza Parkway, Paramus.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.paramus4thofjuly.com/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eParamus Independence Day Parade\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. The annual Independence Day Parade in Paramus on July 4  will feature participates like local first responders, community organizations and more. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eBegins at 9 a.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at the intersection of Farview Avenue and E. Century Road, moving north on Farview Avenue. It will conclude at the Memorial Elementary School on Midland Avenue.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRidgefield\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.ridgefieldpark.org/fourth-july-committee\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRidgefield Park July 4th Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Ridgefield Park will have festivities all day on July 4th, including a reading of the Declaration of Independence, a flag raising ceremony and a parade. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 7:30 a.m.\u003cstrong\u003e Go: \u003c/strong\u003eMemorial Plaza 554 Shaler Blvd., Ridgefield Park.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRidgewood\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.ridgewoodjuly4th.com/schedule\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRidgewood 114th Annual Fourth of July Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. This all-day event on July 4th features a flag raising at Wilsey Square followed by a parade starting at Monroe Street and Godwin Avenue. Then, there will be evening entertainment, food trucks and a beer garden at Veterans Field, followed by the National Anthem and a fireworks show. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eFlag raising begins at 9 a.m.; parade begins at 10 a.m.; evening entertainment begins at 6 p.m.; and the National Anthem and fireworks begin at 9 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eVeterans Field, 156-158 Northern Parkway, Ridgewood.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRiver Edge\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.riveredgenj.org/events/28810/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRiver Edge July 4th Parade and Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. The events will include a parade on July 4 throughout River Edge, as well as a fair with a variety of vendors. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: S\u003c/strong\u003etarts at 11 a.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eParade begins on Cherry Hill and ends at Memorial Park on Continental Avenue.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/21/fourth-of-july-fireworks-2024-north-jersey-things-to-do/73640506007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eFourth of July events in North Jersey kick off June 26. Here\u0026#39;s where to catch them all\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMorris County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eDover\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.dover.nj.us/cn/eventscalendar/eventdetail.cfm?eid\u003d100159\u0026tpid\u003d18150\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDover July 4th Fireworks and Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Dover will be hosting a July 4th celebration with food, activities, live entertainment and fireworks on July 3. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 6 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e302 E. McFarlan St., Dover.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eFlorham Park\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.fpjuly4th.com/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFlorham Park July 4th Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. During this full day of celebration on July 4, there will be a flag raising ceremony at the Florham Park Fire Department at 315 Brooklake Road, followed by the annual town parade. Then, rides, food, games and more will be available at Emmett Park Field, with fireworks in the evening. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e9 a.m. to 9:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eEmmett Park Field, 111 Ridgedale Ave., Florham Park.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eHanover\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.hanovertownship.com/DocumentCenter/View/6002/Patriotic-Celebration-2024-SAVE-THE-DATE?bidId\u003d\"\u003eHanover Township Patriotic Celebration\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e. Hanover Township is holding their 2024 Patriotic Celebration, which will feature food trucks, live music, games, face painting, balloon art and fireworks. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e 6 to 10 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Hanover Township Municipal Complex, 1000 Route 10, Whippany.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLake Hopatcong\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7794720002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.lhyc.com/events-fireworks\"\u003eLake Hopatcong Annual Fourth of July Fireworks\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e. The Lake Hopatcong Yacht Club will be hosting their annual July 4th fireworks on June 28 on the main lake of Lake Hopatcong. Parking will be available on Bertrand Island for residents and members only. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e9:30 to 10:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e75 North Bertrand Road, Mount Arlington. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMontville\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://montville4th.com/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMontville 4th of July Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. From June 26 through June 28, Montville will be hosting their annual 4th of July celebration events. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://montville4th.com/#schedule\"\u003eEach day\u003c/a\u003e features different attractions, including food and beer trucks, carnival rides, live entertainment, a car show and fireworks. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eOpen 5 to 10 p.m. each day. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eMontville Township High School, 100 Horseneck Road, Montville.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMorris Plains\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://morrisplainsboro.org/family-day-and-fireworks/\"\u003eMorris Plains Family Day and Fireworks\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e. The annual Morris Plains Family Day will be held at Morris Plains Community Park on June 29, featuring food, activities and entertainment. Then, their July 4th fireworks show will take place after sundown. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eFamily Day begins at 5 p.m., and the fireworks begin around 9:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e51 Jim Fear Dr., Morris Plains.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMountain Lakes \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://mtnlakes.org/event/july-4th-fireworks/#:~:text\u003d9pm%3A%20Fireworks%20display%20will%20take,and%20consider%20walking%20or%20carpooling.\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMountain Lakes July 4th Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. A festive July 4th fireworks show will take place July 2 over Mountain Lake, and Island Beach will be open for viewing. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 9 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e276 Boulevard, Mountain Lakes.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRandolph\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://k06783.site.kiwanis.org/2022-randolph-freedom-festival/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRandolph Freedom Festival\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Held from July 11 to 13, the Randolph Freedom Festival will feature live music, games, food, a beer garden and fireworks. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e6 to 11 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e214 Center Grove Road, Randolph.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePassaic County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBloomingdale\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tapinto.net/towns/tri-borough/sections/arts-and-entertainment/articles/bloomingdale-borough-releases-2024-schedule\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBloomingdale July 4th Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Bloomingdale will host their annual July 4th fireworks show on June 29 at Walter T. Bergen School. The event will also feature food and rides. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 6 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e225 Glenwild Ave., Bloomingdale.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eClifton\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://cliftonnj.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID\u003d30579\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eClifton Independence Day Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. The event on July 6 will feature a festival with food vendors, activities, games, rides, music and more, followed by a fireworks show. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Starts at 4 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e350 Piaget Ave., Clifton.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7794284001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePaterson\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/fireworks-and-food-truck-festival-tickets-923138972517\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePaterson Food Truck Festival and Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Visitors are invited to enjoy food from local businesses, as well as a fireworks display, on June 30. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 5 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Great Falls Welcome Center, 65 McBride Ave. Extension.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSussex County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eAugusta\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://sussexcountyminers.com/sussex-county-miners-unveil-largest-promo-schedule-to-date/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eJuly 4th Hometown Heroes Parade and Sussex County Miners Game\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. In Augusta on July 4, events include the Hometown Heroes Parade, a game between the Sussex County Miners and the New Jersey Jackals, as well as a fireworks display. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 4:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e94 Championship Place, Augusta.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMontague\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://montaguenj.org/departments___services/montague_day/index.php\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMontague Day and July 4th Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Montague Day on June 29 will feature the Miss Montague Contest, an animal exhibit, live entertainment, a cornhole tournament, a dunk tank, vendors, food, fireworks after dark and more. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e The event starts at 4 p.m., and the fireworks begin after dark. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Montague Town Hall, 227 Clover Road, Montague.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eEssex County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBloomfield\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://essexcountynj.org/event/essex-county-2024-summer-concert-series/\"\u003eEssex County Summer Concert Series and Fireworks\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/strong\u003e Listen to the Infernos at Brookdale Park, and enjoy a fireworks show, on July 3. The Infernos’ repertoire includes big band, oldies, Motown and today’s chart hits. Founded by the late Bobby Wells, former musical director of the Duprees, the band features lead singer Kenny Simmons, formerly of the Commodores. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 7:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e 473 Watchung Ave., Bloomfield.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eCedar Grove\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://cedargrovenj.org/2024/05/29/2024-fireworks-display/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCedar Grove Annual Fireworks Display\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Cedar Grove is hosting their annual Fourth of July fireworks display and celebration event July 1, which features a live DJ, a balloon artist, a patriotic obstacle course, crafts and refreshments. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Starts at 7 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003ePanther Park Field, 118 W Bradford Ave., Cedar Grove.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLivingston\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://redirect.viglink.com/?format\u003dgo\u0026jsonp\u003dvglnk_171535843732910\u0026key\u003d21da03b4eb74bdb05e3c34be1129f465\u0026libId\u003dlw0vvsuc0103k1tf000ULbicdku2n\u0026loc\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.new-jersey-leisure-guide.com%2Fjuly-4.html\u0026v\u003d1\u0026opt\u003dtrue\u0026out\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.livingstonnj.org%2Fcalendar.aspx%3FEID%3D5086\u0026ref\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2F\u0026title\u003dBest%20July%204%20Fireworks%20Celebrations%20in%20New%20Jersey%3A%202024%20Edition\u0026txt\u003dVisit%20their%20site%20to%20learn%20more\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLivingston July 4th Community Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. This all-day event on July 4 will feature a car show, food trucks, games, live entertainment and a beer garden. The celebration will conclude with Livingston\u0026#39;s annual fireworks show. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e9 a.m. to 9:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eMemorial Oval, Robert H. Harp Drive, Livingston.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "1563341001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMontclair\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.montclairnjusa.org/Visitors/Things-to-Do/Special-Events/July-4th-Celebrations\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMontclair July 4th celebrations\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. The series of celebrations taking place in Montclair on July 4th include the town\u0026#39;s 68th annual July 4th parade, followed by a family picnic in Edgemont Park and a fireworks display at Yogi Berra Stadium on the Montclair State University campus. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Parade begins at 11 a.m., followed by the family picnic; fireworks begin around sundown. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eParade begins at South Fullerton Avenue and Bloomfield Avenue and travels to Edgemont Park; Edgemont Park, Valley Road and Holland Terrace, Montclair.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNewark\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca style\u003d\"font-weight: bold;\" href\u003d\"https://essexcountynj.org/event/essex-county-2024-summer-concert-series/\"\u003eEssex County Free Summer Concert Series\u003c/a\u003e will include two free performances in Newark featuring fireworks displays. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Both concerts begin at 7:30 p.m.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe New Jersey Symphony Orchestra will perform on June 28. The program will feature a medley of classics, Broadway themes and patriotic favorites; as well as John Williams’ Liberty Fanfare, John Philip Sousa’s Atlantic City Pageant March and other Jersey treasures. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e The Great Lawn at Branch Brook Park, Heller Parkway. In case of rain, the concert will be relocated to the Jim Wise Theatre in Kupfrian Hall on Summit Street on the campus of NJIT.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMen of Soul will perform soul and R\u0026amp;B music on July 2. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eWeequahic Park, Elizabeth and Meeker avenues.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNutley\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.nutleynj.org/events/78312/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNutley Fourth of July Celebration and Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. In Nutley, July 4th festivities include a variety of food vendors, liv music, games and a fireworks show. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Celebration events start at 6:30 p.m. and fireworks begin at dusk. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Nutley Park Oval, 300 Franklin Ave. Nutley.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eVerona\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.veronanj.org/calendar\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVerona Fourth of July Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Verona\u0026#39;s Fourth of July event on June 28 will include a night full of dancing with a DJ and other live entertainment, as well as a fireworks show at dusk. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 7 pm. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Verona Community Center, 880 Bloomfield Ave., Verona.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eHudson County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eJersey City\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.jerseycityculture.org/july-4th-fireworks-celebration-returns-to-jersey-city/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eJersey City 4th of July Celebrations\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. At Exchange Place Path Plaza, there will be a variety of activities on July 4th, include the Jersey City Night Market, carnival rides, games, live music and food vendors. Then, enjoy the annual Macy\u0026#39;s July 4th fireworks on the Hudson River. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eNoon to 10 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e68 Christopher Columbus Drive, Jersey City.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73976509007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIndependence Day will be here before we know it, so it\u0026#39;s time to start planning how you\u0026#39;d like to celebrate. And, while attending a family gathering or a backyard barbecue could be fun, there\u0026#39;s nothing quite like ringing in the Fourth of July with some fireworks, parades, festivals and more.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBecause North Jersey has celebrations taking place in every corner of the region, we\u0026#39;ve compiled a list of the currently scheduled events to make your life easier.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd you won\u0026#39;t want to miss the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.macys.com/s/fireworks/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ethe 48th Annual Macy\u0026#39;s Fourth of July Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. While this event is technically in New York City, the Macy\u0026#39;s July 4th fireworks will \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/new-jersey/2024/04/30/macys-july-4th-fireworks-return-hudson-river-nj-nyc/73518682007/\"\u003etake place on the Hudson River for the first time since 2013\u003c/a\u003e, meaning New Jersey residents can view them from places like Hoboken, Jersey City and Weehawken. The show begins at 8 p.m. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHere\u0026#39;s a look at the Fourth of July events and firework shows taking place across North Jersey in 2024, by location.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003eWant to see them filtered by date? Head on over to our other story: \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/21/fourth-of-july-fireworks-2024-north-jersey-things-to-do/73640506007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/21/fourth-of-july-fireworks-2024-north-jersey-things-to-do/73640506007/\"\u003eWhen are North Jersey fireworks?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBergen County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eCresskill\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cresskillboro.com/index.php/component/fileman/?view\u003dfile\u0026routed\u003d1\u0026itemless\u003d1\u0026name\u003dJuly%204th%20Celebration%202024.pdf\u0026folder\u003d2024/06\u0026container\u003dfileman-files\"\u003e4th of July Townwide Celebration\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e. On July 4 (rain date July 5), enjoy a day of fun, food, rides, games, a D.J. and more. Call the Recreation Office at 201-816-8065 or jmitchell@cresskillboro.org for information. Cresskill residents only. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e 10 a.m. to 1 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eCommunity Center, 100 Third St.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eEast Rutherford\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://playmeadowlands.com/event/fan-appreciation-fireworks-night/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMeadowlands Fireworks \u0026amp; Fan Appreciation Night\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. At Fan Appreciation Night at Meadowlands Racetrack on July 6you enjoy $1 concession items, $2 Bud and Bud Light drafts, as well as a free fireworks show for July 4th after the races. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e6 to 11:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eMeadowlands Racetrack, 1 Racetrack Drive, East Rutherford.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eEdgewater\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.edgewaternj.org/CivicAlerts.aspx?AID\u003d387\"\u003eIndependence Day Fireworks\u003c/a\u003e. Fireworks, live music, food trucks and kids activities on June 27. Bring a chair or blanket. Parking is limited, so attendees are encouraged to use the free River Road shuttle bus. The rain date is June 30. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e 6 to 10 p.m. Fireworks begin at approximately 9:20. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Veterans Field, 1057-1165 River Road.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eFair Lawn\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.fairlawn.org/p/holiday-events\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFair Lawn Fireworks Show\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Fair Lawn will be hosting their annual fireworks show on June 27. In addition to fireworks, there will be food vendors and live music for guests to enjoy. Tickets for the pre-fireworks festivities are $5 for children under 12 and seniors, $7 for adults and $25 for a family of five. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eGates for the event open at 6:45 p.m., and fireworks begin at sundown. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eMemorial Park, Berdan Avenue and 1st Street, Fair Lawn.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGlen Rock\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"http://www.glenrockpops.org\"\u003ePops Celebrates Nation’s Birthday\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/strong\u003e The Pops Orchestra goes patriotic on July 3 with a free concert on the lawn of Borough Hall. Bring chairs and blankets, and enjoy the music that will include an evening of marches, popular patriotic songs and light classics under the baton of music director Anthony LaGruth. Meet the grand marshals – Marcia, Walter and Daniel Perry - of the July 4 parade as well. The IDA raffle drawing will take place during the intermission, with prizes including a $500 Visa gift card and a $250 Shop the Rock basket of gift cards from town merchants. Tickets will be available for purchase at Kilroy’s prior to the concert or at Borough Hall that night. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eConcert begins at 7 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eBorough Hall, 1 Harding Plaza.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHere Comes the Parade on July 4th.\u003c/strong\u003e Rain or shine, there will be marching bands, pipers, historic Civil War reenactors, floats, clowns and more. For information, write to grparade@icloud.com. \u003cstrong\u003eHours\u003c/strong\u003e: The parade kicks off at 9:30 a.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e The route begins at Glen Rock High School, 400 Hamilton Ave., and goes east on Harristown Road, takes a left on Highland Road, another left at Rock Road through the center of town, and a right on Doremus Avenue, ending at the Municipal Pool parking lot. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLeonia\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.co.bergen.nj.us/public-information/press-releases/768-county-nj-wind-symphony-partner-to-bring-4th-of-july-concert-fireworks-to-overpeck-county-park\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBergen County\u0026#39;s Star-Spangled Spectacular\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. This Independence Day celebration on July 4 will feature the New Jersey Wind Symphony, other live entertainment, children\u0026#39;s activities, food trucks, a beer and wine garden and fireworks at Overpeck Creek. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 5 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eOverpeck County Park, 40 Fort Lee Road, Leonia.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLyndhurst\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://allevents.in/lyndhurst/zappy-4th-of-july/200026427019623#google_vignette\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLyndhurst\u0026#39;s Zappy Fourth of July\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. At the Lyndhurst Band Shell, there will be a free concert on July 4 with several different performers to celebrate the Fourth of July. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e 7:30 to 9 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eLyndhurst Municipal Park, 367 Valley Brook Ave., Lyndhurst.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eParamus\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7862975002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.paramus4thofjuly.com/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eParamus 4th of July Fireworks Show\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Paramus will be hosting their annual 4th of July fireworks show on June 30. Prior to the fireworks show, there will be live entertainment and food vendors. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e The time of the event is to be determined. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Cliff Gennarelli Sports Complex, Garden State Plaza Parkway, Paramus.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.paramus4thofjuly.com/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eParamus Independence Day Parade\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. The annual Independence Day Parade in Paramus on July 4  will feature participates like local first responders, community organizations and more. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eBegins at 9 a.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at the intersection of Farview Avenue and E. Century Road, moving north on Farview Avenue. It will conclude at the Memorial Elementary School on Midland Avenue.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRidgefield\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.ridgefieldpark.org/fourth-july-committee\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRidgefield Park July 4th Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Ridgefield Park will have festivities all day on July 4th, including a reading of the Declaration of Independence, a flag raising ceremony and a parade. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 7:30 a.m.\u003cstrong\u003e Go: \u003c/strong\u003eMemorial Plaza 554 Shaler Blvd., Ridgefield Park.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRidgewood\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.ridgewoodjuly4th.com/schedule\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRidgewood 114th Annual Fourth of July Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. This all-day event on July 4th features a flag raising at Wilsey Square followed by a parade starting at Monroe Street and Godwin Avenue. Then, there will be evening entertainment, food trucks and a beer garden at Veterans Field, followed by the National Anthem and a fireworks show. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eFlag raising begins at 9 a.m.; parade begins at 10 a.m.; evening entertainment begins at 6 p.m.; and the National Anthem and fireworks begin at 9 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eVeterans Field, 156-158 Northern Parkway, Ridgewood.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRiver Edge\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.riveredgenj.org/events/28810/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRiver Edge July 4th Parade and Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. The events will include a parade on July 4 throughout River Edge, as well as a fair with a variety of vendors. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: S\u003c/strong\u003etarts at 11 a.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eParade begins on Cherry Hill and ends at Memorial Park on Continental Avenue.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/21/fourth-of-july-fireworks-2024-north-jersey-things-to-do/73640506007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eFourth of July events in North Jersey kick off June 26. Here\u0026#39;s where to catch them all\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMorris County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eDover\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.dover.nj.us/cn/eventscalendar/eventdetail.cfm?eid\u003d100159\u0026tpid\u003d18150\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDover July 4th Fireworks and Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Dover will be hosting a July 4th celebration with food, activities, live entertainment and fireworks on July 3. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 6 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e302 E. McFarlan St., Dover.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eFlorham Park\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.fpjuly4th.com/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFlorham Park July 4th Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. During this full day of celebration on July 4, there will be a flag raising ceremony at the Florham Park Fire Department at 315 Brooklake Road, followed by the annual town parade. Then, rides, food, games and more will be available at Emmett Park Field, with fireworks in the evening. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e9 a.m. to 9:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eEmmett Park Field, 111 Ridgedale Ave., Florham Park.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eHanover\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.hanovertownship.com/DocumentCenter/View/6002/Patriotic-Celebration-2024-SAVE-THE-DATE?bidId\u003d\"\u003eHanover Township Patriotic Celebration\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e. Hanover Township is holding their 2024 Patriotic Celebration, which will feature food trucks, live music, games, face painting, balloon art and fireworks. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e 6 to 10 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Hanover Township Municipal Complex, 1000 Route 10, Whippany.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLake Hopatcong\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7794720002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.lhyc.com/events-fireworks\"\u003eLake Hopatcong Annual Fourth of July Fireworks\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e. The Lake Hopatcong Yacht Club will be hosting their annual July 4th fireworks on June 28 on the main lake of Lake Hopatcong. Parking will be available on Bertrand Island for residents and members only. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e9:30 to 10:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e75 North Bertrand Road, Mount Arlington. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMontville\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://montville4th.com/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMontville 4th of July Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. From June 26 through June 28, Montville will be hosting their annual 4th of July celebration events. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://montville4th.com/#schedule\"\u003eEach day\u003c/a\u003e features different attractions, including food and beer trucks, carnival rides, live entertainment, a car show and fireworks. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eOpen 5 to 10 p.m. each day. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eMontville Township High School, 100 Horseneck Road, Montville.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMorris Plains\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://morrisplainsboro.org/family-day-and-fireworks/\"\u003eMorris Plains Family Day and Fireworks\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e. The annual Morris Plains Family Day will be held at Morris Plains Community Park on June 29, featuring food, activities and entertainment. Then, their July 4th fireworks show will take place after sundown. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eFamily Day begins at 5 p.m., and the fireworks begin around 9:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e51 Jim Fear Dr., Morris Plains.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMountain Lakes \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://mtnlakes.org/event/july-4th-fireworks/#:~:text\u003d9pm%3A%20Fireworks%20display%20will%20take,and%20consider%20walking%20or%20carpooling.\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMountain Lakes July 4th Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. A festive July 4th fireworks show will take place July 2 over Mountain Lake, and Island Beach will be open for viewing. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 9 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e276 Boulevard, Mountain Lakes.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRandolph\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://k06783.site.kiwanis.org/2022-randolph-freedom-festival/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRandolph Freedom Festival\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Held from July 11 to 13, the Randolph Freedom Festival will feature live music, games, food, a beer garden and fireworks. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e6 to 11 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e214 Center Grove Road, Randolph.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePassaic County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBloomingdale\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tapinto.net/towns/tri-borough/sections/arts-and-entertainment/articles/bloomingdale-borough-releases-2024-schedule\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBloomingdale July 4th Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Bloomingdale will host their annual July 4th fireworks show on June 29 at Walter T. Bergen School. The event will also feature food and rides. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 6 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e225 Glenwild Ave., Bloomingdale.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eClifton\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://cliftonnj.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID\u003d30579\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eClifton Independence Day Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. The event on July 6 will feature a festival with food vendors, activities, games, rides, music and more, followed by a fireworks show. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Starts at 4 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e350 Piaget Ave., Clifton.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7794284001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePaterson\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/fireworks-and-food-truck-festival-tickets-923138972517\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePaterson Food Truck Festival and Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Visitors are invited to enjoy food from local businesses, as well as a fireworks display, on June 30. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 5 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Great Falls Welcome Center, 65 McBride Ave. Extension.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSussex County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eAugusta\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://sussexcountyminers.com/sussex-county-miners-unveil-largest-promo-schedule-to-date/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eJuly 4th Hometown Heroes Parade and Sussex County Miners Game\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. In Augusta on July 4, events include the Hometown Heroes Parade, a game between the Sussex County Miners and the New Jersey Jackals, as well as a fireworks display. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 4:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e94 Championship Place, Augusta.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMontague\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://montaguenj.org/departments___services/montague_day/index.php\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMontague Day and July 4th Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Montague Day on June 29 will feature the Miss Montague Contest, an animal exhibit, live entertainment, a cornhole tournament, a dunk tank, vendors, food, fireworks after dark and more. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e The event starts at 4 p.m., and the fireworks begin after dark. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Montague Town Hall, 227 Clover Road, Montague.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eEssex County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBloomfield\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://essexcountynj.org/event/essex-county-2024-summer-concert-series/\"\u003eEssex County Summer Concert Series and Fireworks\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/strong\u003e Listen to the Infernos at Brookdale Park, and enjoy a fireworks show, on July 3. The Infernos’ repertoire includes big band, oldies, Motown and today’s chart hits. Founded by the late Bobby Wells, former musical director of the Duprees, the band features lead singer Kenny Simmons, formerly of the Commodores. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 7:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e 473 Watchung Ave., Bloomfield.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eCedar Grove\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://cedargrovenj.org/2024/05/29/2024-fireworks-display/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCedar Grove Annual Fireworks Display\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Cedar Grove is hosting their annual Fourth of July fireworks display and celebration event July 1, which features a live DJ, a balloon artist, a patriotic obstacle course, crafts and refreshments. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Starts at 7 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003ePanther Park Field, 118 W Bradford Ave., Cedar Grove.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLivingston\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://redirect.viglink.com/?format\u003dgo\u0026jsonp\u003dvglnk_171535843732910\u0026key\u003d21da03b4eb74bdb05e3c34be1129f465\u0026libId\u003dlw0vvsuc0103k1tf000ULbicdku2n\u0026loc\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.new-jersey-leisure-guide.com%2Fjuly-4.html\u0026v\u003d1\u0026opt\u003dtrue\u0026out\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.livingstonnj.org%2Fcalendar.aspx%3FEID%3D5086\u0026ref\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2F\u0026title\u003dBest%20July%204%20Fireworks%20Celebrations%20in%20New%20Jersey%3A%202024%20Edition\u0026txt\u003dVisit%20their%20site%20to%20learn%20more\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLivingston July 4th Community Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. This all-day event on July 4 will feature a car show, food trucks, games, live entertainment and a beer garden. The celebration will conclude with Livingston\u0026#39;s annual fireworks show. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e9 a.m. to 9:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eMemorial Oval, Robert H. Harp Drive, Livingston.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "1563341001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMontclair\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.montclairnjusa.org/Visitors/Things-to-Do/Special-Events/July-4th-Celebrations\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMontclair July 4th celebrations\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. The series of celebrations taking place in Montclair on July 4th include the town\u0026#39;s 68th annual July 4th parade, followed by a family picnic in Edgemont Park and a fireworks display at Yogi Berra Stadium on the Montclair State University campus. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Parade begins at 11 a.m., followed by the family picnic; fireworks begin around sundown. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eParade begins at South Fullerton Avenue and Bloomfield Avenue and travels to Edgemont Park; Edgemont Park, Valley Road and Holland Terrace, Montclair.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNewark\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca style\u003d\"font-weight: bold;\" href\u003d\"https://essexcountynj.org/event/essex-county-2024-summer-concert-series/\"\u003eEssex County Free Summer Concert Series\u003c/a\u003e will include two free performances in Newark featuring fireworks displays. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Both concerts begin at 7:30 p.m.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe New Jersey Symphony Orchestra will perform on June 28. The program will feature a medley of classics, Broadway themes and patriotic favorites; as well as John Williams’ Liberty Fanfare, John Philip Sousa’s Atlantic City Pageant March and other Jersey treasures. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e The Great Lawn at Branch Brook Park, Heller Parkway. In case of rain, the concert will be relocated to the Jim Wise Theatre in Kupfrian Hall on Summit Street on the campus of NJIT.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMen of Soul will perform soul and R\u0026amp;B music on July 2. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eWeequahic Park, Elizabeth and Meeker avenues.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNutley\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.nutleynj.org/events/78312/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNutley Fourth of July Celebration and Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. In Nutley, July 4th festivities include a variety of food vendors, liv music, games and a fireworks show. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Celebration events start at 6:30 p.m. and fireworks begin at dusk. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Nutley Park Oval, 300 Franklin Ave. Nutley.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eVerona\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.veronanj.org/calendar\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVerona Fourth of July Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Verona\u0026#39;s Fourth of July event on June 28 will include a night full of dancing with a DJ and other live entertainment, as well as a fireworks show at dusk. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 7 pm. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Verona Community Center, 880 Bloomfield Ave., Verona.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eHudson County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eJersey City\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.jerseycityculture.org/july-4th-fireworks-celebration-returns-to-jersey-city/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eJersey City 4th of July Celebrations\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. At Exchange Place Path Plaza, there will be a variety of activities on July 4th, include the Jersey City Night Market, carnival rides, games, live music and food vendors. Then, enjoy the annual Macy\u0026#39;s July 4th fireworks on the Hudson River. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eNoon to 10 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e68 Christopher Columbus Drive, Jersey City.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73976509007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIndependence Day will be here before we know it, so it\u0026#39;s time to start planning how you\u0026#39;d like to celebrate. And, while attending a family gathering or a backyard barbecue could be fun, there\u0026#39;s nothing quite like ringing in the Fourth of July with some fireworks, parades, festivals and more.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBecause North Jersey has celebrations taking place in every corner of the region, we\u0026#39;ve compiled a list of the currently scheduled events to make your life easier.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd you won\u0026#39;t want to miss the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.macys.com/s/fireworks/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ethe 48th Annual Macy\u0026#39;s Fourth of July Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. While this event is technically in New York City, the Macy\u0026#39;s July 4th fireworks will \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/new-jersey/2024/04/30/macys-july-4th-fireworks-return-hudson-river-nj-nyc/73518682007/\"\u003etake place on the Hudson River for the first time since 2013\u003c/a\u003e, meaning New Jersey residents can view them from places like Hoboken, Jersey City and Weehawken. The show begins at 8 p.m. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHere\u0026#39;s a look at the Fourth of July events and firework shows taking place across North Jersey in 2024, by location.  \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003eWant to see them filtered by date? Head on over to our other story: \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/21/fourth-of-july-fireworks-2024-north-jersey-things-to-do/73640506007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/21/fourth-of-july-fireworks-2024-north-jersey-things-to-do/73640506007/\"\u003eWhen are North Jersey fireworks?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBergen County\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eCresskill\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cresskillboro.com/index.php/component/fileman/?view\u003dfile\u0026routed\u003d1\u0026itemless\u003d1\u0026name\u003dJuly%204th%20Celebration%202024.pdf\u0026folder\u003d2024/06\u0026container\u003dfileman-files\"\u003e4th of July Townwide Celebration\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e. On July 4 (rain date July 5), enjoy a day of fun, food, rides, games, a D.J. and more. Call the Recreation Office at 201-816-8065 or jmitchell@cresskillboro.org for information. Cresskill residents only. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e 10 a.m. to 1 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eCommunity Center, 100 Third St.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eEast Rutherford\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://playmeadowlands.com/event/fan-appreciation-fireworks-night/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMeadowlands Fireworks \u0026amp; Fan Appreciation Night\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. At Fan Appreciation Night at Meadowlands Racetrack on July 6you enjoy $1 concession items, $2 Bud and Bud Light drafts, as well as a free fireworks show for July 4th after the races. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e6 to 11:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eMeadowlands Racetrack, 1 Racetrack Drive, East Rutherford.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eEdgewater\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.edgewaternj.org/CivicAlerts.aspx?AID\u003d387\"\u003eIndependence Day Fireworks\u003c/a\u003e. Fireworks, live music, food trucks and kids activities on June 27. Bring a chair or blanket. Parking is limited, so attendees are encouraged to use the free River Road shuttle bus. The rain date is June 30. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e 6 to 10 p.m. Fireworks begin at approximately 9:20. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Veterans Field, 1057-1165 River Road.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eFair Lawn\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.fairlawn.org/p/holiday-events\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFair Lawn Fireworks Show\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Fair Lawn will be hosting their annual fireworks show on June 27. In addition to fireworks, there will be food vendors and live music for guests to enjoy. Tickets for the pre-fireworks festivities are $5 for children under 12 and seniors, $7 for adults and $25 for a family of five. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eGates for the event open at 6:45 p.m., and fireworks begin at sundown. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eMemorial Park, Berdan Avenue and 1st Street, Fair Lawn.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGlen Rock\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"http://www.glenrockpops.org\"\u003ePops Celebrates Nation’s Birthday\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/strong\u003e The Pops Orchestra goes patriotic on July 3 with a free concert on the lawn of Borough Hall. Bring chairs and blankets, and enjoy the music that will include an evening of marches, popular patriotic songs and light classics under the baton of music director Anthony LaGruth. Meet the grand marshals – Marcia, Walter and Daniel Perry - of the July 4 parade as well. The IDA raffle drawing will take place during the intermission, with prizes including a $500 Visa gift card and a $250 Shop the Rock basket of gift cards from town merchants. Tickets will be available for purchase at Kilroy’s prior to the concert or at Borough Hall that night. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eConcert begins at 7 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eBorough Hall, 1 Harding Plaza.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHere Comes the Parade on July 4th.\u003c/strong\u003e Rain or shine, there will be marching bands, pipers, historic Civil War reenactors, floats, clowns and more. For information, write to grparade@icloud.com. \u003cstrong\u003eHours\u003c/strong\u003e: The parade kicks off at 9:30 a.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e The route begins at Glen Rock High School, 400 Hamilton Ave., and goes east on Harristown Road, takes a left on Highland Road, another left at Rock Road through the center of town, and a right on Doremus Avenue, ending at the Municipal Pool parking lot. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLeonia\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.co.bergen.nj.us/public-information/press-releases/768-county-nj-wind-symphony-partner-to-bring-4th-of-july-concert-fireworks-to-overpeck-county-park\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBergen County\u0026#39;s Star-Spangled Spectacular\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. This Independence Day celebration on July 4 will feature the New Jersey Wind Symphony, other live entertainment, children\u0026#39;s activities, food trucks, a beer and wine garden and fireworks at Overpeck Creek. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 5 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eOverpeck County Park, 40 Fort Lee Road, Leonia.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLyndhurst\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://allevents.in/lyndhurst/zappy-4th-of-july/200026427019623#google_vignette\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLyndhurst\u0026#39;s Zappy Fourth of July\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. At the Lyndhurst Band Shell, there will be a free concert on July 4 with several different performers to celebrate the Fourth of July. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e 7:30 to 9 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eLyndhurst Municipal Park, 367 Valley Brook Ave., Lyndhurst.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eParamus\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "7862975002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.paramus4thofjuly.com/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eParamus 4th of July Fireworks Show\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Paramus will be hosting their annual 4th of July fireworks show on June 30. Prior to the fireworks show, there will be live entertainment and food vendors. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e The time of the event is to be determined. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Cliff Gennarelli Sports Complex, Garden State Plaza Parkway, Paramus.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.paramus4thofjuly.com/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eParamus Independence Day Parade\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. The annual Independence Day Parade in Paramus on July 4  will feature participates like local first responders, community organizations and more. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eBegins at 9 a.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at the intersection of Farview Avenue and E. Century Road, moving north on Farview Avenue. It will conclude at the Memorial Elementary School on Midland Avenue.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRidgefield\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.ridgefieldpark.org/fourth-july-committee\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRidgefield Park July 4th Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Ridgefield Park will have festivities all day on July 4th, including a reading of the Declaration of Independence, a flag raising ceremony and a parade. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 7:30 a.m.\u003cstrong\u003e Go: \u003c/strong\u003eMemorial Plaza 554 Shaler Blvd., Ridgefield Park.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRidgewood\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.ridgewoodjuly4th.com/schedule\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRidgewood 114th Annual Fourth of July Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. This all-day event on July 4th features a flag raising at Wilsey Square followed by a parade starting at Monroe Street and Godwin Avenue. Then, there will be evening entertainment, food trucks and a beer garden at Veterans Field, followed by the National Anthem and a fireworks show. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eFlag raising begins at 9 a.m.; parade begins at 10 a.m.; evening entertainment begins at 6 p.m.; and the National Anthem and fireworks begin at 9 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eVeterans Field, 156-158 Northern Parkway, Ridgewood.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRiver Edge\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.riveredgenj.org/events/28810/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRiver Edge July 4th Parade and Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. The events will include a parade on July 4 throughout River Edge, as well as a fair with a variety of vendors. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: S\u003c/strong\u003etarts at 11 a.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eParade begins on Cherry Hill and ends at Memorial Park on Continental Avenue.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/21/fourth-of-july-fireworks-2024-north-jersey-things-to-do/73640506007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eFourth of July events in North Jersey kick off June 26. Here\u0026#39;s where to catch them all\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMorris County\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eDover\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.dover.nj.us/cn/eventscalendar/eventdetail.cfm?eid\u003d100159\u0026tpid\u003d18150\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDover July 4th Fireworks and Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Dover will be hosting a July 4th celebration with food, activities, live entertainment and fireworks on July 3. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 6 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e302 E. McFarlan St., Dover.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eFlorham Park\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.fpjuly4th.com/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFlorham Park July 4th Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. During this full day of celebration on July 4, there will be a flag raising ceremony at the Florham Park Fire Department at 315 Brooklake Road, followed by the annual town parade. Then, rides, food, games and more will be available at Emmett Park Field, with fireworks in the evening. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e9 a.m. to 9:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eEmmett Park Field, 111 Ridgedale Ave., Florham Park.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eHanover\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.hanovertownship.com/DocumentCenter/View/6002/Patriotic-Celebration-2024-SAVE-THE-DATE?bidId\u003d\"\u003eHanover Township Patriotic Celebration\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e. Hanover Township is holding their 2024 Patriotic Celebration, which will feature food trucks, live music, games, face painting, balloon art and fireworks. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e 6 to 10 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Hanover Township Municipal Complex, 1000 Route 10, Whippany.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLake Hopatcong\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "7794720002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.lhyc.com/events-fireworks\"\u003eLake Hopatcong Annual Fourth of July Fireworks\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e. The Lake Hopatcong Yacht Club will be hosting their annual July 4th fireworks on June 28 on the main lake of Lake Hopatcong. Parking will be available on Bertrand Island for residents and members only. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e9:30 to 10:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e75 North Bertrand Road, Mount Arlington. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMontville\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://montville4th.com/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMontville 4th of July Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. From June 26 through June 28, Montville will be hosting their annual 4th of July celebration events. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://montville4th.com/#schedule\"\u003eEach day\u003c/a\u003e features different attractions, including food and beer trucks, carnival rides, live entertainment, a car show and fireworks. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eOpen 5 to 10 p.m. each day. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eMontville Township High School, 100 Horseneck Road, Montville.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMorris Plains\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://morrisplainsboro.org/family-day-and-fireworks/\"\u003eMorris Plains Family Day and Fireworks\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e. The annual Morris Plains Family Day will be held at Morris Plains Community Park on June 29, featuring food, activities and entertainment. Then, their July 4th fireworks show will take place after sundown. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eFamily Day begins at 5 p.m., and the fireworks begin around 9:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e51 Jim Fear Dr., Morris Plains.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMountain Lakes \u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://mtnlakes.org/event/july-4th-fireworks/#:~:text\u003d9pm%3A%20Fireworks%20display%20will%20take,and%20consider%20walking%20or%20carpooling.\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMountain Lakes July 4th Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. A festive July 4th fireworks show will take place July 2 over Mountain Lake, and Island Beach will be open for viewing. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 9 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e276 Boulevard, Mountain Lakes.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRandolph\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://k06783.site.kiwanis.org/2022-randolph-freedom-festival/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRandolph Freedom Festival\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Held from July 11 to 13, the Randolph Freedom Festival will feature live music, games, food, a beer garden and fireworks. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e6 to 11 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e214 Center Grove Road, Randolph.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePassaic County\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBloomingdale\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tapinto.net/towns/tri-borough/sections/arts-and-entertainment/articles/bloomingdale-borough-releases-2024-schedule\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBloomingdale July 4th Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Bloomingdale will host their annual July 4th fireworks show on June 29 at Walter T. Bergen School. The event will also feature food and rides. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 6 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e225 Glenwild Ave., Bloomingdale.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eClifton\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://cliftonnj.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID\u003d30579\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eClifton Independence Day Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. The event on July 6 will feature a festival with food vendors, activities, games, rides, music and more, followed by a fireworks show. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Starts at 4 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e350 Piaget Ave., Clifton.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "7794284001"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePaterson\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/fireworks-and-food-truck-festival-tickets-923138972517\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePaterson Food Truck Festival and Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Visitors are invited to enjoy food from local businesses, as well as a fireworks display, on June 30. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 5 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Great Falls Welcome Center, 65 McBride Ave. Extension.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSussex County\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eAugusta\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://sussexcountyminers.com/sussex-county-miners-unveil-largest-promo-schedule-to-date/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eJuly 4th Hometown Heroes Parade and Sussex County Miners Game\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. In Augusta on July 4, events include the Hometown Heroes Parade, a game between the Sussex County Miners and the New Jersey Jackals, as well as a fireworks display. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 4:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e94 Championship Place, Augusta.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMontague\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://montaguenj.org/departments___services/montague_day/index.php\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMontague Day and July 4th Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Montague Day on June 29 will feature the Miss Montague Contest, an animal exhibit, live entertainment, a cornhole tournament, a dunk tank, vendors, food, fireworks after dark and more. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e The event starts at 4 p.m., and the fireworks begin after dark. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Montague Town Hall, 227 Clover Road, Montague.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eEssex County\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBloomfield\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://essexcountynj.org/event/essex-county-2024-summer-concert-series/\"\u003eEssex County Summer Concert Series and Fireworks\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/strong\u003e Listen to the Infernos at Brookdale Park, and enjoy a fireworks show, on July 3. The Infernos’ repertoire includes big band, oldies, Motown and today’s chart hits. Founded by the late Bobby Wells, former musical director of the Duprees, the band features lead singer Kenny Simmons, formerly of the Commodores. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 7:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e 473 Watchung Ave., Bloomfield.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eCedar Grove\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://cedargrovenj.org/2024/05/29/2024-fireworks-display/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCedar Grove Annual Fireworks Display\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Cedar Grove is hosting their annual Fourth of July fireworks display and celebration event July 1, which features a live DJ, a balloon artist, a patriotic obstacle course, crafts and refreshments. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Starts at 7 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003ePanther Park Field, 118 W Bradford Ave., Cedar Grove.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLivingston\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://redirect.viglink.com/?format\u003dgo\u0026jsonp\u003dvglnk_171535843732910\u0026key\u003d21da03b4eb74bdb05e3c34be1129f465\u0026libId\u003dlw0vvsuc0103k1tf000ULbicdku2n\u0026loc\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.new-jersey-leisure-guide.com%2Fjuly-4.html\u0026v\u003d1\u0026opt\u003dtrue\u0026out\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.livingstonnj.org%2Fcalendar.aspx%3FEID%3D5086\u0026ref\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2F\u0026title\u003dBest%20July%204%20Fireworks%20Celebrations%20in%20New%20Jersey%3A%202024%20Edition\u0026txt\u003dVisit%20their%20site%20to%20learn%20more\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLivingston July 4th Community Celebration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. This all-day event on July 4 will feature a car show, food trucks, games, live entertainment and a beer garden. The celebration will conclude with Livingston\u0026#39;s annual fireworks show. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003e9 a.m. to 9:30 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eMemorial Oval, Robert H. Harp Drive, Livingston.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "1563341001"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMontclair\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.montclairnjusa.org/Visitors/Things-to-Do/Special-Events/July-4th-Celebrations\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMontclair July 4th celebrations\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. The series of celebrations taking place in Montclair on July 4th include the town\u0026#39;s 68th annual July 4th parade, followed by a family picnic in Edgemont Park and a fireworks display at Yogi Berra Stadium on the Montclair State University campus. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Parade begins at 11 a.m., followed by the family picnic; fireworks begin around sundown. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eParade begins at South Fullerton Avenue and Bloomfield Avenue and travels to Edgemont Park; Edgemont Park, Valley Road and Holland Terrace, Montclair.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNewark\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca style\u003d\"font-weight: bold;\" href\u003d\"https://essexcountynj.org/event/essex-county-2024-summer-concert-series/\"\u003eEssex County Free Summer Concert Series\u003c/a\u003e will include two free performances in Newark featuring fireworks displays. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Both concerts begin at 7:30 p.m.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe New Jersey Symphony Orchestra will perform on June 28. The program will feature a medley of classics, Broadway themes and patriotic favorites; as well as John Williams’ Liberty Fanfare, John Philip Sousa’s Atlantic City Pageant March and other Jersey treasures. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e The Great Lawn at Branch Brook Park, Heller Parkway. In case of rain, the concert will be relocated to the Jim Wise Theatre in Kupfrian Hall on Summit Street on the campus of NJIT.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eMen of Soul will perform soul and R\u0026amp;B music on July 2. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eWeequahic Park, Elizabeth and Meeker avenues.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNutley\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.nutleynj.org/events/78312/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNutley Fourth of July Celebration and Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. In Nutley, July 4th festivities include a variety of food vendors, liv music, games and a fireworks show. \u003cstrong\u003eHours:\u003c/strong\u003e Celebration events start at 6:30 p.m. and fireworks begin at dusk. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Nutley Park Oval, 300 Franklin Ave. Nutley.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eVerona\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.veronanj.org/calendar\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVerona Fourth of July Fireworks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. Verona\u0026#39;s Fourth of July event on June 28 will include a night full of dancing with a DJ and other live entertainment, as well as a fireworks show at dusk. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eStarts at 7 pm. \u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Verona Community Center, 880 Bloomfield Ave., Verona.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eHudson County\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eJersey City\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.jerseycityculture.org/july-4th-fireworks-celebration-returns-to-jersey-city/\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eJersey City 4th of July Celebrations\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. At Exchange Place Path Plaza, there will be a variety of activities on July 4th, include the Jersey City Night Market, carnival rides, games, live music and food vendors. Then, enjoy the annual Macy\u0026#39;s July 4th fireworks on the Hudson River. \u003cstrong\u003eHours: \u003c/strong\u003eNoon to 10 p.m. \u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e68 Christopher Columbus Drive, Jersey City.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "71894400007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe first Broadway revival of Samm-Art Williams’ “Home” is full of joy and pain, heart and hope.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd sorrow, for the playwright passed away days before the first preview. But rest assured Williams is smiling from above after every performance, for this atypical work is engrossing and entertaining   \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe story is about Cephus Miles (Tory Kittles), a Black farmer in North Carolina. He’s in love with Pattie Mae (Brittany Inge), who goes off to college. But things take a turn when he is thrown in jail for opposing the Vietnam War draft. And when he moves to the big city, his life becomes dangerous and complicated.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDirected by the Tony Award-winning Kenny Leon, the script in this 90-minute show is packed with poetry, melody, rhythm and song. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74048330007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere\u0026#39;s talk of land, soil, sun, rain and crops. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eGod, faith and family — and America.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere are dozens of characters, but only three people in this small-scale but mighty production. The acting is first-rate. Stori Ayers is identified as Woman Two in the program, but she portrays everyone from a a youngster to a prison guard to a bus driver. Watching her transform from one moment to the next is one of the highlights of the night.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe audience warms up to Kittles quickly. He allows us to share Cephus\u0026#39; tragedy as he goes from the comforts of home to jail to being lost among the masses, peddling for cash any way he can.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eInge plays multiple characters, too, but she shines bright as Pattie Mae. Maybe it\u0026#39;s her eyes? Her smile? There\u0026#39;s real chemistry between Inge and Kittles that is wonderful to see.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74048433007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe minimal set by Arnulfo Maldonado works, as does lighting by Allen Lee Hughes, costumes by Dede Ayite, sound design by Justin Ellington, and hair and wig design by Nikiya Mathis. Kate Wilson deserves mention as voice coach.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEverything comes together to make this a feel-good evening. The ending may be predictable, but that’s OK.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“Home” opens the 2024-25 season, and it’s timing could not be better. What are the tens of thousands of migrants looking for? Jobs, opportunities, a place to start again.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe work also gives voice to the poor and lonely and homeless — and anyone in America looking for a place to fit in, to belong. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd it\u0026#39;s a reminder that no matter how far away we go, we can’t escape who we are, where we come from.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHome will always be a part of us.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "12148395002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo\u003c/strong\u003e: “Home,” through July 21, Todd Haimes Theatre, 227 W. 42nd St., New York, $49 to $149; 212-719-1300, roundabouttheatre.org.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eBill Canacci can be reached at \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"mailto:bcanacci@gannettnj.com\"\u003e\u003cem\u003ebcanacci@gannettnj.com\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "71894400007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe first Broadway revival of Samm-Art Williams’ “Home” is full of joy and pain, heart and hope.\u003c/p\u003e"
